{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"tail -6 agent/tree_screen_resumed.log; tail -5 agent/stack_daily_dense_ranks.log; tail -4 agent/lead_temporal_dense.log; sed -n '65,140p' agent/report.md; cat agent/BUDGET.md\"","aggregated_output":"dev2 XAU 86400: 60 prompts, 3 variants\nNVDAX filled 40/40 price-gap prompts from validator realized paths\ndev2 NVDAX 86400: 60 prompts, 3 variants\nGOOGLX filled 60/60 price-gap prompts from validator realized paths\ndev2 GOOGLX 86400: 60 prompts, 3 variants\nTSLAX filled 57/57 price-gap prompts from validator realized paths\ndev1/stacked/com-equ-24h {'reward_rank': 129, 'final_rank': 150, 'miners': 257, 'reward_ratio': 0.014075454322068713, 'reward_rounds': 1499, 'first_round': '2026-07-28 00:13:00+00:00', 'last_round': '2026-08-06 23:50:00+00:00'}\ndev1/stacked/crypto-24h {'reward_rank': 62, 'final_rank': 93, 'miners': 257, 'reward_ratio': 0.21822163758436092, 'reward_rounds': 1015, 'first_round': '2026-07-28 00:13:00+00:00', 'last_round': '2026-08-06 23:59:00+00:00'}\n- Phase  : normal\n\nHYPE filled 14/14 price-gap prompts from validator realized paths\nXAU filled 104/104 price-gap prompts from validator realized paths\n\n## Results\n\nFull 1000-path starter replays produce Score estimates **0.32375** and **0.42456** on the two development windows.\n\nFull official reward replay supports the current temporal/Sobol incumbent:\n\n| Window | Competition | Starter reward rank | Incumbent reward rank | Incumbent reward / best field reward |\n|---|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| dev1 | COM_EQU_24H | 239 / 257 | 129 / 257 | 0.014075 |\n| dev1 | CRYPTO_1H | 216 / 257 | 25 / 257 | 0.869436 |\n| dev1 | CRYPTO_24H | 236 / 257 | 62 / 257 | 0.218222 |\n| dev2 | COM_EQU_24H | 248 / 257 | 216 / 257 | 0.009365 |\n| dev2 | CRYPTO_1H | 227 / 257 | 14 / 257 | 0.872234 |\n| dev2 | CRYPTO_24H | 257 / 257 | 163 / 257 | 0.126951 |\n\nThese correspond to development Score estimates **36.724** and **33.618**, versus 0.32375 and 0.42456 for the starter. It is substantial progress, but not cumulative field leadership. The hourly final-round ranks are 60 and 1, distinct from cumulative ranks 25 and 14. Commodity/equity emissions remain particularly weak. Each row uses all official reward rounds for its selected candidate; hourly has 1,624/1,847 post-warmup rounds, daily crypto 1,015/1,044, and COM_EQU 1,499/1,474. Production and research paths match to relative tolerance 1e-12 on representative assets and both formats. The reserved final validation remains untouched.\n\nThese are historical reward estimates, not the campaign's eventual post-cutoff Score. Sampled terminal-rank diagnostics and reward-round-thinned screens are explicitly labeled and are not substituted for full final replay.\n\n## Limitations\n\n- The effective validation sample consists of market days and regimes, not thousands of independent prompt observations. Overlapping horizons create dependence.\n- Many hypotheses are screened on the same development windows. The reserved final window remains necessary, and small grid gains may be selection noise.\n- Internal likelihood diagnostics split rows by prediction timestamp; adjacent 24-hour targets can overlap at that split boundary. They are model-selection diagnostics, not causal field backtests. Every field-scored forecast starts after the entire fitting-label cutoff.\n- Response curves around already fitted parameters are meta-training objectives, not claims of causal historical forecasting performance. All reported candidate CRPS and rewards are evaluated later through the official scorer.\n- The pinned configuration uses ten-day daily and five-day hourly smoothing windows. Default backtester warmup trimming therefore gives different effective reward intervals; reports must state those intervals rather than repeat the campaign prose's 24-hour description.\n- The official backtester may replace NaN-holed realized paths with cached validator truth. This behavior is preserved, not silently altered.\n- A context with no finite positive close cannot supply the required starting price; the model raises a clear error instead of inventing one.\n- The frozen-data interface does not provide contemporaneous cross-asset information or external news. Additional information used by live miners may not be reproducible here.\n- A bounded historical score-only API probe returned out-of-request timestamps and was rejected before any score analysis or storage. Evaluation remains strictly offline, with a fail-closed environment check.\n\n## What we would do with more budget\n\nThe campaign still has budget and is continuing. Priorities are to confirm temporal/lead interactions, finish finite-ensemble and hourly emission-sensitive selection, and stress-test chronological calibration. Any additional fitted checkpoint must be available before the predictions it evaluates. Final nomination requires a frozen model, a full 1000-path field replay with explicit warmup handling, interface checks, and committed artifacts—not an attractive development-only CRPS table.\n# BUDGET — maintained by the harness (read-only for you)\n\n- Credits: 52.03 / 100.00 USD (52%)\n- Time   : 0.1 h elapsed, 17.9 h remaining (1%)\n- Phase  : normal\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
