{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/journal.md\n@@\n # Research journal — campaign-3\n+\n+## Iteration 39 — persistent Student scale process (preregistered)\n+\n+- Hypothesis: a single shared Student scale for an entire 24-hour path overstates the persistence of uncertainty; earlier IID-tail and lognormal-volatility experiments also changed the one-step marginal family, so they did not isolate this question.\n+- Change: retain the exact baseline Sobol Gaussian increments and five-degree Student scale marginal. Evolve the scale's Gaussian-copula latent once per forecast hour, with exponential correlation times of 6 or 24 hours, using a separately scrambled Sobol stream. Every step retains the same marginal scale distribution; only scale dependence across hours changes. Keep static/temporal forecasts, clock, lead shape and field windows fixed.\n+- Result: pending 1000-path daily official CRPS on both development windows.\n+- Verdict: require consistent gains; otherwise retain the simpler shared path scale. No claim that matching one-step marginals guarantees matching longer-horizon distributions.\n+- Lesson: pending.\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/sampling.py\n@@\n-from scipy.special import ndtri\n+from scipy.special import ndtr, ndtri\n@@\n def mixture_shocks(count, steps, seed, mode, degrees=5.):\n@@\n     return np.concatenate([shocks, -shocks], axis=0)[:count]\n+\n+\n+def persistent_shocks(count, steps, seed, increment, persistence_minutes):\n+    if steps == 0 or np.isinf(persistence_minutes):\n+        return mixture_shocks(count, steps, seed, 'sobol')\n+    pairs = (count+1)//2\n+    power = int(np.ceil(np.log2(max(1, pairs))))\n+    engine = qmc.Sobol(steps+1, scramble=True, seed=int(seed % (2**32)))\n+    uniforms = engine.random_base2(power)[:pairs]\n+    normals = ndtri(np.clip(uniforms[:, 1:], 1e-12, 1-1e-12))\n+    block_indices = np.arange(steps)*increment//3600\n+    blocks = int(block_indices[-1]+1)\n+    scale = np.empty((pairs, blocks))\n+    scale[:, 0] = np.sqrt(3/chi2.ppf(np.clip(uniforms[:, 0], 1e-12, 1-1e-12), 5))\n+    if blocks > 1:\n+        innovations = qmc.Sobol(blocks-1, scramble=True, seed=int((seed \"'^ 0x6A09E667) % (2**32)))\n+        innovations = ndtri(np.clip(innovations.random_base2(power)[:pairs], 1e-12, 1-1e-12))\n+        latent = ndtri(np.clip(uniforms[:, 0], 1e-12, 1-1e-12))\n+        correlation = np.exp(-60/persistence_minutes)\n+        for block in range(1, blocks):\n+            latent = correlation*latent+np.sqrt(1-correlation**2)*innovations[:, block-1]\n+            scale[:, block] = np.sqrt(3/chi2.ppf(np.clip(ndtr(latent), 1e-12, 1-1e-12), 5))\n+    shocks = normals*scale[:, block_indices]\n+    return np.concatenate([shocks, -shocks], axis=0)[:count]\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/research.py\n@@\n-    stacked_mode = parts[0] in ['\"'stacked','refresh','refresh_old','stacktick','stackdf','stackperiodic','stackensemble','stacktree','stacklead']\n+    stacked_mode = parts[0] in ['stacked','refresh','refresh_old','stacktick','stackdf','stackperiodic','stackensemble','stacktree','stacklead','stackpersist']\n+    sampler_persistence = float(parts[1]) if parts[0]=='stackpersist' else None\n@@\n         shocks = mixture_shocks(count, steps, draw_seed, sampler, sampler_degrees)\n+        if sampler_persistence is not None:\n+            from sampling import persistent_shocks\n+\n+            shocks = persistent_shocks(count, steps, draw_seed, increment, sampler_persistence)\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\nOMP_NUM_THREADS=1 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 uv run agent/research.py --name persistence_screen --variants stacked,stackpersist:360,stackpersist:1440 --format low --paths 1000 --workers 2 --resume > agent/persistence_screen.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
