{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_81","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat agent/auxiliary.py; cat agent/BUDGET.md; tail -3 agent/tree_daily_dense.log; tail -4 agent/stack_mix_dense.log; tail -3 agent/fit_newton_score.log'","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"NaN-tolerant, scale-normalized features from optional candle information.\"\"\"\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nHALF_LIVES = (30,60,180,360,720,1440,2880,10080)\n\n\ndef auxiliary_features(context,timestamp,reference,absolute):\n    age=(pd.Timestamp(timestamp)-context.index).total_seconds().to_numpy()/60\n    valid_count=max(int(context.close.notna().sum()),1)\n    vector=[]\n    usable=False\n    if {'high','low'}.issubset(context.columns):\n        high=pd.to_numeric(context.high,errors='coerce').to_numpy(dtype=float)\n        low=pd.to_numeric(context.low,errors='coerce').to_numpy(dtype=float)\n        valid=np.isfinite(high)&np.isfinite(low)&(low>0)&(high>=low)\n        ranges=np.log(high[valid]/low[valid])\n        usable=bool((ranges>0).sum()>20 and valid.sum()/valid_count>.5)\n    else:\n        valid=np.zeros(len(context),dtype=bool)\n        ranges=np.array([])\n    for half_life in HALF_LIVES:\n        scale=absolute[half_life]\n        if usable:\n            weights=np.exp(-np.log(2)*age[valid]/half_life)\n            scale=float(np.average(ranges,weights=weights)*np.sqrt(np.pi/8))\n        vector.append(np.log(max(scale,1e-9)/max(reference,1e-8)))\n    vector.append(min(1.,valid.sum()/valid_count))\n    for column in ['volume','trade_count']:\n        values=pd.to_numeric(context[column],errors='coerce').to_numpy(dtype=float) if column in context else np.full(len(context),np.nan)\n        valid_values=np.isfinite(values)&(values>=0)\n        if valid_values.sum()>20 and np.any(values[valid_values]>0):\n            means=[]\n            for half_life in [60,360,1440,10080]:\n                weights=np.exp(-np.log(2)*age[valid_values]/half_life)\n                means.append(float(np.average(values[valid_values],weights=weights)))\n            vector.extend(np.log((np.asarray(means[:3])+1e-8)/(means[-1]+1e-8)))\n            vector.extend([np.log1p(means[-1]),min(1.,valid_values.sum()/valid_count)])\n        else:\n            vector.extend([0.]*5)\n    return np.asarray(vector,dtype=np.float32),usable\n# BUDGET — maintained by the harness (read-only for you)\n\n- Credits: 56.58 / 100.00 USD (57%)\n- Time   : 0.3 h elapsed, 17.7 h remaining (2%)\n- Phase  : normal\nAAPLX filled 240/240 price-gap prompts from validator realized paths\ndev2 AAPLX 86400: 240 prompts, 1 variants\nWTIOIL filled 98/98 price-gap prompts from validator realized paths\ndev2 NVDAX 86400: 240 prompts, 5 variants\nSP500 filled 60/60 price-gap prompts from validator realized paths\ndev2 GOOGLX 86400: 240 prompts, 5 variants\ndev2 TSLAX 86400: 240 prompts, 5 variants\nSOL 685 curves\nBTC 701 curves\nXAU 352 curves\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_70","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/journal.md\n@@\n # Research journal — campaign-3\n+\n+### Iteration 40 field fidelity\n+\n+The numerical student preserves the teacher's daily gains at 1000 paths. Student CRPS ratios are COM_EQU 0.998859/0.997996 and crypto 0.999453/0.999113, versus teacher 0.998860/0.997989 and 0.999325/0.999171. The student artifact is about 1.7 MiB versus the pretrained cache's 183 MiB, and it does not invoke pretrained inference. Proceed to dense confirmation rather than declare equivalence from a sparse mean alone.\n+\n+## Iteration 41 — daily component interactions (preregistered)\n+\n+- Hypothesis: a tree correction to overall scale and a temporal correction to relative lead shape are complementary; the separate periodic level correction may instead duplicate clock information in the tree.\n+- Change: use the distilled tree, promoted temporal lead and GCD projection. Evaluate every daily development prompt at 1000 paths for the student alone, lead plus projection, and student plus lead plus projection. For COM_EQU only, also test adding the already-screened half-periodic correction to each lead-containing combination. No hourly changes, new fitting labels or final-window inspection.\n+- Result: pending dense official CRPS and reward replay.\n+- Verdict: retain components only if their incremental joint effect survives both regimes. Screen rewards with thinned rounds to avoid replaying clearly inferior combinations, then confirm the selected joint model at every official round before promotion.\n+- Lesson: pending. Individual improvements are not assumed additive.\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/research.py\n@@\n-    stacked_mode = parts[0] in ['stacked','refresh','refresh_old','stacktick','stackdf','stackperiodic','stackensemble','stacktree','stacklead','stackpersist','stackstudent']\n+    stacked_mo