{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_120","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/journal.md\n@@\n # Research journal — campaign-3\n+\n+## Iteration 47 — rank-based marginal stratification (preregistered)\n+\n+- Hypothesis: even the Sobol fan retains finite-sample marginal error. Replacing each sampled marginal with evenly spaced quantiles of the intended Student distribution may reduce this error without fitting another predictor.\n+- Change: preserve sample ranks and all current scale/shape forecasts. Separately remap standardized single-step shocks, or cumulative log-price deviations using their known cumulative diffusion scale, onto midpoint quantiles of the five-degree Student family. Test half/full remapping strengths against exact zero-strength control at 1000 paths, both development windows and all three competitions. The ordering comes only from our own simulated samples, never from future prices or other miners.\n+- Result: pending official CRPS. This changes the finite fan's joint behavior as well as targeted marginals; it is not assumed to preserve every scored increment distribution exactly.\n+- Verdict: require both-window improvement and official rewards before promotion. Do not optimize random seeds or add further quantile grids after seeing field results.\n+- Lesson: pending.\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/sampling.py\n@@\n from collections import deque\n+from functools import lru_cache\n@@\n-from scipy.stats import chi2, qmc\n+from scipy.stats import chi2, qmc, t\n@@\n def persistent_shocks(count, steps, seed, increment, persistence_minutes):\n@@\n     return np.concatenate([shocks, -shocks], axis=0)[:count]\n+\n+\n+@lru_cache(maxsize=8)\n+def student_quantiles(count, degrees=5.):\n+    probabilities = (np.arange(count)+.5)/count\n+    return np.sqrt((degrees-2)/degrees)*t.ppf(probabilities, degrees)\n+\n+\n+def stratified_marginals(values, scales=1.):\n+    if values.shape[1] == 0:\n+        return values.copy()\n+    order = np.argsort(values, axis=0, kind='stable')\n+    output = np.empty_like(values)\n+    np.put_along_axis(output, order, student_quantiles(len(values))[:, None], axis=0)\n+    return output*np.broadcast_to(scales, (values.shape[1],))\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/research.py\n@@\n-    stacked_mode = parts[0] in ['stacked','refresh','refresh_old','stacktick','stackdf','stackperiodic','stackensemble','stacktree','stacklead','stackpersist','stackstudent','stackmix','stacknewton','stackfine']\n-    fine_strength = float(parts[1]) if parts[0]=='stackfine' else None\n+    stacked_mode = parts[0] in ['stacked','refresh','refresh_old','stacktick','stackdf','stackperiodic','stackensemble','stacktree','stacklead','stackpersist','stackstudent','stackmix','stacknewton','stackfine','stackrank']\n+    rank_mode = parts[1] if parts[0]=='stackrank' else None\n+    rank_strength = float(parts[2]) if rank_mode else 0.\n+    fine_strength = (1. if asset not in CRYPTO and length>3600 else None) if parts[0]=='stackrank' else float(parts[1]) if parts[0]=='stackfine' else None\n@@\n-    temporal_lead_strength = 1. if parts[0] in ['stacknewton','stackfine'] else float(parts[2]) if parts[0]=='stackmix' else float(parts[1]) if parts[0]=='stacklead' else None\n-    tree_strength = 1. if parts[0]=='stackfine' else float(parts[1]) if parts[0] in ['stacktree','stackstudent','stackmix'] else None\n+    temporal_lead_strength = 1. if parts[0] in ['stacknewton','stackfine','stackrank'] else float(parts[2]) if parts[0]=='stackmix' else float(parts[1]) if parts[0]=='stacklead' else None\n+    tree_strength = (1. if length>3600 else None) if parts[0]=='stackrank' else 1. if parts[0]=='stackfine' else float(parts[1]) if parts[0] in ['stacktree','stackstudent','stackmix'] else None\n@@\n-    tree_kind = 'tree_student' if parts[0] in ['stackstudent','stackmix','stackfine'] else 'tree'\n+    tree_kind = 'tree_student' if parts[0]