{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_212","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/report.md\n@@\n-For a fixed continuous predictive distribution, an equally weighted finite ensemble at midpoint quantiles minimizes expected empirical-ensemble CRPS. This is a property of the submitted finite distribution, not evidence that its underlying forecast is correct. Zamo and Naveau (2018), *Estimation of the Continuous Ranked Probability Score with Limited Information and Applications to Ensemble Weather Forecasts*, Mathematical Geosciences, DOI \"'`10.1007/s11004-017-9709-7`, discuss this distinction in Section 3.2.1 and attribute the optimal quantile result to Bröcker (2012).\n+For a fixed continuous predictive distribution with a finite first moment, an equally weighted finite ensemble at midpoint quantiles minimizes expected empirical-ensemble CRPS when observations follow that distribution. This is a property of the submitted finite distribution, not evidence that its underlying forecast is correct. Zamo and Naveau (2018), *Estimation of the Continuous Ranked Probability Score with Limited Information and Applications to Ensemble Weather Forecasts*, Mathematical Geosciences, DOI `10.1007/s11004-017-9709-7`, discuss this distinction in Section 3.2.1 and attribute the optimal quantile result to Bröcker (2012).\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\napply_patch <<'\"'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/journal.md\n@@\n # Research journal — campaign-3\n+\n+### Warmed replay reconstruction and day-level stability\n+\n+Reconstructing all three warmed incumbent competitions from their saved official CRPS gives exactly the original ratios, ranks and retained intervals: COM_EQU 0.04673687382620357, hourly crypto 0.8953589120219363, daily crypto 0.34199446651969584. Thus candidate reward replay has an exact golden baseline rather than merely a similar aggregate. The stratified candidate is still running.\n+\n+On August 8–18, increment/prefix stratification improves every asset's aggregate CRPS. Its asset-mean daily ratio improves on 9/10 COM_EQU days, 9/10 hourly-crypto days and 10/10 daily-crypto days. These are descriptive paired-day checks, not independent-sample significance tests; overlapping forecasts remain dependent. The publisher's full text confirms the finite-ensemble quantile reference; no market data was accessed online.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\ncat agent/BUDGET.md; tail -6 agent/rank_warm_compare.log; tail -5 agent/phase_crypto_rewards.log; tail -4 agent/multiscale_dense.log; tail -3 agent/weekly_lead_screen.log\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
