{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_217","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/journal.md\n@@\n # Research journal — campaign-3\n+\n+### Iteration 45 final verdict — reject both phase corrections\n+\n+Despite better mean CRPS, both phase candidates lose dev1 rewards against the deployed daily crypto model's 0.395023 ratio. The aligned control gives 0.384724/0.246129, ranks 39/82; shifted training gives 0.352926/0.270314, ranks 44/78. Dev2 improves against 0.241880, but the preregistered both-window reward gate fails. Discard both corrections entirely, with no asset-specific salvage. This is another concrete counterexample to equating asset-mean CRPS improvement with emissions improvement; it also prevents an unsupported claim that shifted training clocks solve the field problem.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\nOMP_NUM_THREADS=1 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 uv run python - <<'PY'\nimport sys\nimport pandas as pd\nimport numpy as np\nsys.path.insert(0,'agent')\nfrom predict import AGENT_DIR,parallel_combined\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.result import BacktestResult\nfrom synth_lib.backtester.config import competition_for\nroot=AGENT_DIR/'results'/'incumbent_warm_dev2'/'dev2'\nstart=pd.Timestamp('2026-08-08',tz='UTC')\nfor assets,length in [(['BTC','ETH','SOL','XRP','HYPE'],3600),(['XAU','NVDAX','GOOGLX','TSLAX','AAPLX','WTIOIL','SPCX','SP500'],86400)]:\n    original=[]\n    filtered=[]\n    for asset in assets:\n        label=f'{asset}_{length}'\n        prompts=pd.read_parquet(root/f'{label}_prompts.parquet')\n        rounds=pd.read_parquet(root/f'{label}_smoothed.parquet',columns=['updated_at']).drop_duplicates().sort_values('updated_at').iloc[::150]\n        original.append(BacktestResult('original',prompts,rounds,{}))\n        filtered.append(BacktestResult('filtered',prompts,rounds.loc[rounds.updated_at>=start],{}))\n    config=competition_for(assets[0],length)\n    before=parallel_combined(original,config,workers=3)\n    before=before.loc[before.updated_at>=start].sort_values(['updated_at','miner_uid']).reset_index(drop=True)\n    after=parallel_combined(filtered,config,workers=3).sort_values(['updated_at','miner_uid']).reset_index(drop=True)\n    pd.testing.assert_frame_equal(before,after)\n    print('Identical retained official rounds with early filtering:',length,len(after),flush=True)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
