{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_237","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/modeling.py\n@@\n-from scipy.stats import chi2, qmc, t\n+from scipy.stats import chi2, qmc, t as student_t\n@@\n-    return np.sqrt(3/5)*t.ppf(probabilities,5)\n+    return np.sqrt(3/5)*student_t.ppf(probabilities,5)\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\napply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/.gitignore\n@@\n agent/results/phase_training.npz\n+agent/results/fast_training.npz\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\napply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/report.md\n@@\n-| Randomized training-clock coverage | Narrowly passes the paired likelihood gate; crypto field gains are not uniformly better than the aligned-clock control. Dense comparison is underway. |\n-| Marginal rank stratification | Daily increment and hourly prefix remapping improve every-prompt CRPS in both development windows; warmed official reward confirmation is underway. |\n+| Randomized training-clock coverage | Both shifted and aligned controls improve mean daily crypto CRPS, but both lose dev1 rewards; reject both. |\n+| Marginal rank stratification | Daily increment and hourly prefix remapping pass dense CRPS and full reward confirmation. Hourly prefix remapping is promoted. |\n+| Multiscale daily stratification | Two fixed fine-to-coarse sweeps improve on increment-only remapping in both daily competitions/windows; dense CRPS and warmed rewards confirm promotion. |\n+| Smooth weekly lead shape | Passes its chronological likelihood gate and first field screen; dense confirmation remains active. |\n+| Sub-hour scale features | Added 5/15/30-minute information improves likelihood only 0.000366 beyond the matched control, below its 0.0005 gate; rejected before field scoring. |\n@@\n The first/last retained reward timestamps are August 8 00:36–August 17 23:56 UTC for commodities/equities, August 8 00:08–August 17 23:57 for hourly crypto, and August 8 00:48–August 17 23:31 for daily crypto. These explicitly warmed results are not interchangeable with the short-window development table. The active field count also changes. All use 1000 paths and the official backtester.\n+\n+The promoted finite-fan construction raises the explicitly warmed Score estimate to **45.030144**. It uses multiscale daily projection and hourly prefix stratification, with no new fitted weights:\n+\n+| Competition | Cumulative reward rank | Reward / best field reward |\n+|---|---:|---:|\n+| COM_EQU_24H | 161 / 252 | 0.0510693 |\n+| CRYPTO_1H | 9 / 257 | 0.9206018 |\n+| CRYPTO_24H | 61 / 257 | 0.3792333 |\n+\n+These use exactly the retained rounds and intervals described for the warmed baseline. Reconstruction from saved official CRPS reproduces every baseline ratio and rank exactly before candidate comparison. The same sampler changes give a dev1 short-window Score proxy of **49.830242**, with ranks 108/257, 21/257 and 32/257 in the table's competition order. These two numbers use different warmup protocols and should not be averaged.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\ngit add -u\ngit ls-files --others --exclude-standard -z agent | xargs -0 -r git add --\ngit commit -m 'Promote multiscale daily and prefix hourly fans after exact warmed reward confirmation'\ncat agent/BUDGET.md; tail -6 agent/stale_age_screen.log; tail -4 agent/weekly_lead_dense.log\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
