{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_243","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/journal.md\n@@\n # Research journal — campaign-3\n+\n+## Iteration 53 — multi-minute information in official-score calibration (preregistered)\n+\n+- Hypothesis: the fitted numerical design describes minute-return volatility but does not directly encode how returns aggregate over 5/15/30 minutes. Nine ratios across 1h/6h/24h memories may reveal conditional microstructure effects relevant to daily scoring.\n+- Change: rebuild the three-point 0.92/1/1.08 scale-response curves around the promoted multiscale daily model, using the same pre-field training anchors and 1000-path official scorer. Apply scaling inside the generator before the lattice, correcting the old calibration experiment's approximate post-generation scaling. Fit matched ridge Newton controls with and without nine multi-minute/minute absolute-volatility ratios. Select identity or penalty 0.001/0.01/0.1/1 solely on the chronological quadratic diagnostic; keep +/-8% bounds. Then rescore both selected fits and identity through the official scorer on the actual diagnostic contexts.\n+- Result: pending. This is a controlled feature ablation on a refreshed, correctly projected score-response objective, not reuse of the old score curves as if the serving model were unchanged.\n+- Verdict: a daily competition proceeds to development only if the richer design improves actual diagnostic CRPS by at least 0.0001 against both identity and its matched control. Require both development windows and full rewards before promotion. Do not adopt or retune the control after a failed added-feature gate.\n+- Lesson: pending.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\napply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /workspace/agent/micro_score.py\n+\\\"\\\"\\\"Multi-minute features for a bounded daily score-calibration ablation.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n+\n+from functools import lru_cache\n+from pathlib import Path\n+\n+import numpy as np\n+\n+from newton_score import newton_design\n+\n+\n+def micro_design(feature, asset, timestamp):\n+    extra = [np.log(max(feature[f'av{lag}'][half_life],1e-9)/max(feature['av'][half_life],1e-9))\n+             for lag in [5,15,30] for half_life in [60,360,1440]]\n+    return np.r_[newton_design(feature,asset,timestamp),np.clip(extra,-4,4)]\n+\n+\n+@lru_cache(maxsize=2)\n+def micro_weights(kind):\n+    with np.load(Path(__file__).with_name(f'micro_{kind}_weights.npz')) as archive:\n+        return dict(archive)\n+\n+\n+def micro_multiplier(feature, asset, timestamp, kind):\n+    weights = micro_weights(kind)\n+    design = micro_design(feature,asset,timestamp) if kind=='extra' else newton_design(feature,asset,timestamp)\n+    design = np.r_[1.,np.clip((design-weights['center'])/weights['spread'],-8,8)]\n+    return 1+np.clip(design @ weights['coefficients'],-.08,.08)\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\napply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/research.py\n@@\n     center_strength = float(parts[1]) if parts[0]=='stackcenter' else 0.\n+    micro_parameters = parts[1:] if parts[0]=='stackmicro' else None\n@@\n-    if parts[0] in ['stackage','stackcenter']:\n+    if parts[0] in ['stackage','stackcenter','stackmicro']:\n@@\n-    innovation = parts[0] if parts[0] in [\\\"iid\\\", \\\"sv\\\", \\\"boot\\\"] else None\n+    if micro_parameters:\n+        if micro_parameters[0]=='constant':\n+            learned_scale *= float(micro_parameters[1])\n+        else:\n+            from micro_score import micro_multiplier\n+\n+            learned_scale *= micro_multiplier(feature,asset,start_time,micro_parameters[0])\n+    innovation = parts[0] if parts[0] in [\\\"iid\\\", \\\"sv\\\", \\\"boot\\\"] else None\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\napply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /workspace/agent/fit_micro_score.py\n+\\\"\\\"\\\"Matched multi-minute ablation using only official finite-fan CRPS.\\\"\\\"\\\"\n+\n+import argparse\n+import hashlib\n+import json\n+from concurrent.futures import ProcessPoolExecutor\n+\n+import numpy as np\n+import pandas as pd\n+\n+from fit_newton_score import weights_for\n+from micro_score import micro_design\n+from predict import AGENT_DIR, ensure_workspace_cwd, load_context, score_paths\n+from research import CRYPTO, EQUITY, features, generate_variant\n+from synth_lib.backtester.preparation import _slice_real_prices\n+\n+\n+def build_asset(task):\n+    asset,verify,fingerprint = task\n+    ensure_workspace_cwd()\n+    checkpoint = AGENT_DIR/'results'/'micro_score.parts'/f'{asset}_{fingerprint}.npz'\n+    if checkpoint.exists() and not verify:\n+        return dict(np.load(checkpoint))\n+    original = np.load(AGENT_DIR/'results'/'volatility_training.npz')\n+    indices = np.load(AGENT_DIR/'results'/'training_score_curves.npz')['indices']\n+    indices = indices[original['inputs'][indices,-13:].argmax(axis=1)==(CRYPTO+EQUITY).index(asset)]\n+    if verify:\n+        indices = indices[original['timestamps'][indices]>=pd.Timestamp('2026-07-01',tz='UTC').value]\n+    timestamps = pd.to_datetime(original['timestamps'][indices],utc=True)\n+    cutoff = pd.Timestamp('2026-07-26',tz='UTC')\n+    prices = load_context(asset,timestamps.min()-pd.Timedelta(days=7),cutoff)\n+    variants = ['stackmicro:constant:1','stackmicro:control','stackmicro:extra'] if verify else [f'stackmicro:constant:{value}' for value in [.92,1.,1.08]]\n+    records = []\n+    for index,timestamp in zip(indices,timestamps):\n+        if timestamp+pd.Timedelta(days=1)>cutoff:\n+            continue\n+        context = prices.loc[(prices.index>timestamp-pd.Timedelta(days=7)) & (prices.index<=timestamp)]\n+        feature = features(context,timestamp,300)\n+        realized = _slice_real_prices(prices[['close']],timestamp,86400,300)\n+        if not np.isfinite(realized[0]) or not np.isfinite(realized[-1]):\n+            continue\n+        scores = [score_paths(generate_variant(feature,asset,timestamp,300,86400,1000,variant),\n+                              realized,300,asset,86400)[0] for variant in variants]\n+        if np.isfinite(scores).all() and min(scores)>0:\n+            records.append((int(index),micro_design(feature,asset,timestamp),scores))\n+    result = {'indices':np.array([row[0] for row in records]),'design':np.stack([row[1] for row in records]),\n+              'scores':np.array([row[2] for row in records])}\n+    if not verify:\n+        checkpoint.parent.mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n+        temporary = checkpoint.with_suffix('.tmp.npz')\n+        np.savez(temporary,**result)\n+        temporary.replace(checkpoint)\n+    print(asset,len(records),'verified' if verify else 'curves',flush=True)\n+    return result\n+\n+\n+def main():\n+    ensure_workspace_cwd()\n+    print((AGENT_DIR/'BUDGET.md').read_text(),flush=True)\n+    parser = argparse.ArgumentParser()\n+    parser.add_argument('--workers',type=int,default=4)\n+    args = parser.parse_args()\n+    fingerprint = hashlib.sha256()\n+    for source in sorted([*AGENT_DIR.glob('*.py'),*[AGENT_DIR/f'{kind}_weights.npz' for kind in\n+                          ['volatility','temporal_exact','lead','lead_temporal','tree_student','periodic','lead_finetune']]]):\n+        fingerprint.update(source.name.encode())\n+        fingerprint.update(source.read_bytes())\n+    digest = fingerprint.hexdigest()\n+    with ProcessPoolExecutor(max_workers=args.workers) as executor:\n+        batches = list(executor.map(build_asset,[(asset,False,digest) for asset in CRYPTO+EQUITY]))\n+    stored = {key:np.concatenate([batch[key] for batch in batches]) for key in ['indices','design','scores']}\n+    np.savez(AGENT_DIR/'results'/'micro_score_training.npz',**stored)\n+    original = np.load(AGENT_DIR/'results'/'volatility_training.npz')\n+    assets = np.asarray(CRYPTO+EQUITY)[original['inputs'][stored['indices'],-13:].argmax(axis=1)]\n+    training = original['timestamps'][stored['indices']]<pd.Timestamp('2026-07-01',tz='UTC').value\n+    scores = stored['scores']\n+    gradient = (scores[:,2]-scores[:,0])/.16\n+    curvature = (scores[:,2]-2*scores[:,1]+scores[:,0])/.08**2\n+    floor = max(float(np.median(curvature[training]))*.001,1e-6)\n+    curvature = np.maximum(curvature,floor)\n+    train_weights,normalizers = weights_for(assets,training,scores[:,1])\n+    diagnostic_weights,_ = weights_for(assets,~training,scores[:,1],normalizers)\n+    diagnostics = {}\n+    choices = {}\n+    for kind,raw_design in [('control',stored['design'][:,:-9]),('extra',stored['design'])]:\n+        center = raw_design[training].mean(axis=0)\n+        spread = np.maximum(raw_design[training].std(axis=0),.1)\n+        design = np.column_stack([np.ones(len(assets)),np.clip((raw_design-center)/spread,-8,8)])\n+        matrix = design.T @ ((train_weights*curvature)[:,None]*design)\n+        direction = -(design.T @ (train_weights*gradient))\n+        best,best_penalty = 0.,None\n+        coefficients = np.zeros(design.shape[1])\n+        for penalty in [.001,.01,.1,1.]:\n+            candidate = np.linalg.solve(matrix+penalty*np.eye(design.shape[1]),direction)\n+            change = np.clip(design @ candidate,-.08,.08)\n+            surrogate = float(diagnostic_weights @ (gradient*change+.5*curvature*change**2))\n+            diagnostics[f'{kind}/{penalty}'] = surrogate\n+            print(kind,penalty,surrogate,flush=True)\n+            if surrogate<best:\n+                best,best_penalty,coefficients = surrogate,penalty,candidate\n+        np.savez(AGENT_DIR/f'micro_{kind}_weights.npz',center=center,spread=spread,coefficients=coefficients)\n+        choices[kind] = {'surrogate_change':best,'penalty':best_penalty}\n+    with ProcessPoolExecutor(max_workers=args.workers) as executor:\n+        batches = list(executor.map(build_asset,[(asset,True,digest) for asset in CRYPTO+EQUITY]))\n+    verified = {key:np.concatenate([batch[key] for batch in batches]) for key in ['indices','scores']}\n+    np.savez(AGENT_DIR/'results'/'micro_score_verification.npz',**verified)\n+    verified_assets = np.asarray(CRYPTO+EQUITY)[original['inputs'][verified['indices'],-13:].argmax(axis=1)]\n+    weights,_ = weights_for(verified_assets,np.ones(len(verified_assets),dtype=bool),verified['scores'][:,0],normalizers)\n+    ratios = {}\n+    for name,group in [('crypto',CRYPTO),('com_equ',EQUITY)]:\n+        selected = np.isin(verified_assets,group)\n+        totals = weights[selected] @ verified['scores'][selected]\n+        ratios[name] = {'control_identity':float(totals[1]/totals[0]),'extra_identity':float(totals[2]/totals[0]),\n+                        'extra_control':float(totals[2]/totals[1]),\n+                        'passed_gate':bool(totals[2]/totals[0]<.9999 and totals[2]/totals[1]<.9999)}\n+    metrics = {'diagnostics':diagnostics,'choices':choices,'verification_ratios':ratios,'curvature_floor':floor,\n+               'training_rows':int(training.sum()),'validation_rows':int((~training).sum()),'paths':1000,\n+               'target_cutoff':'2026-07-26','validation_start':'2026-07-01','fingerprint':digest}\n+    (AGENT_DIR/'micro_score_weights.json').write_text(json.dumps(metrics,indent=2))\n+    print(metrics,flush=True)\n+\n+\n+if __name__=='__main__':\n+    main()\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\nOMP_NUM_THREADS=1 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 uv run agent/fit_micro_score.py --workers 4 > agent/fit_micro_score.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_255","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/journal.md\n@@\n # Research journal — campaign-3\n+\n+### Iteration 49 reward verdict and interface audit\n+\n+Weekly lead shape improves COM_EQU full-round reward ratios to 0.0565473/0.0344222, versus 0.0564549/0.0332406 for its unchanged-sampler baseline; ranks are 111/200 of 257. It loses dev1 crypto rewards (0.3939104 versus 0.395023), despite a tiny positive mean-CRPS result, so reject its crypto branch. The equity branch requires interaction confirmation with the promoted sampler before deployment.\n+\n+The serving audit identifies and fixes a genuine input-type bug: NumPy integer Unix seconds were interpreted as nanoseconds by pandas. Python integers, NumPy integers, floats, ISO strings, naive UTC timestamps and equivalent timezone-aware timestamps now yield identical paths. Reward aggregation now filters unnecessary earlier rounds before official computation and keys its cache by the cutoff. Complete official row comparisons and the exact 42.803008 baseline confirm unchanged retained results.\n+\n+## Iteration 54 — equity weekly-shape/sampler interaction (preregistered)\n+\n+- Hypothesis: the separately confirmed weekly lead shape remains useful with the promoted multiscale daily fan.\n+- Change: combine exactly full-strength weekly lead shape with the fixed two-sweep multiscale sampler, for COM_EQU only. Evaluate every daily development prompt and the entire warmed dev2 input period at 1000 paths, against saved multiscale-only scores. No new strengths or calendar harmonics are introduced.\n+- Result: pending.\n+- Verdict: require both-window mean CRPS gains and full reward improvement before adding the weekly weights to serving. Otherwise retain the simpler promoted sampler.\n+- Lesson: pending.\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\napply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/agent/research.py\n@@\n     micro_parameters = parts[1:] if parts[0]=='stackmicro' else None\n     if parts[0]=='stackweekly':\n-        parts = ['stackrank','increments','0']\n+        parts = ['stackrank',parts[2],'1'] if len(parts)>2 else ['stackrank','increments','0']\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\nOMP_NUM_THREADS=1 OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 uv run agent/research.py --name weekly_joint_dense --windows dev1,warm_dev2 --format low --assets XAU,NVDAX,GOOGLX,TSLAX,AAPLX,WTIOIL,SPCX,SP500 --variants stackweekly:1:multiscale --paths 1000 --stride-low 1 --workers 4 --resume > agent/weekly_joint_dense.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
